{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "title": "Ecco Studio master size roster",
  "approval": "2026-11-08: User approved these sizes through the size audit, two rounds of before/after mockups of 24 screens and per-row decisions. Element types are sized here once; every instance of a type takes these values.",
  "howItWorks": [
    "The size scale lists named sizes in categories (Title, Heading, Text, Control height, Icon, Image). Each element type picks a size by name (\"@heading-2\"); changing a size changes every element that uses it.",
    "Each element entry names the selectors that belong to it. Entries are applied in order; when an element matches several, the later entry wins. Variants refine a type and inherit any size they leave empty.",
    "Edit this file, then run: node scripts/size_roster.mjs. Never edit design-system/sizes.css by hand. Administrators can also edit sizes live in Studio > User Preferences > Look and Feel.",
    "A new element whose type is already here needs no size of its own. A new kind of element must be added here (a type or a variant) with a size from the scale; the ROSTER-01 browser check fails otherwise."
  ],
  "units": "Sizes refer to the scale with \"@id\". A plain number of pixels is allowed for a one-off size; null leaves that property to the element's own styles.",
  "types": [
